# 4.4 Building Panel 3 – HTTP 5xx Error Rate

---

# Objective

The third panel created for the Enterprise Platform Overview dashboard measures the rate of HTTP 5xx server errors generated by the `auth-service`.

Unlike the previous two panels, which measure throughput and performance, this panel measures application reliability.

A healthy application should process requests successfully with minimal server-side failures. A sudden increase in HTTP 5xx responses often indicates application defects, infrastructure failures, dependency outages, or unexpected runtime exceptions.

This panel answers the operational question:

> **Is the application failing to process requests successfully?**

---

# Why This Metric Matters

Monitoring server errors is one of the fastest ways to detect production issues.

An increase in HTTP 5xx responses may indicate:

- Application exceptions
- Database connectivity failures
- External API failures
- Authentication issues
- Thread pool exhaustion
- JVM OutOfMemoryError
- Kubernetes networking problems
- Deployment failures

Even if CPU usage and memory consumption appear normal, a rising 5xx error rate immediately indicates that users are experiencing failures.

